<title>USA: USDA sees record '97 US orange exports to S Korea.</title>
<headline>USDA sees record '97 US orange exports to S Korea.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Thursday U.S. orange exports to South Korea are expected to climb to a record 40,000 tonnes in 1997.</p>
<p>In its World Horticultural Trade and U.S. Export Opportunities report, USDA said U.S. oranges account for virtually all of South Korea's orange imports.</p>
<p>USDA noted under the Uruguay Round agreement, the import quota for oranges was 15,000 tonnes in 1995, 20,000 tonnes in 1996 and 25,000 tonnes for the first six months of 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;Orange imports are expected to total 25,000 tonnes in the first half of 1997 with trade sources expecting imports to reach an additional 15,000 tonnes during the second half of the year,&quot; USDA said in the report.</p>
</text>
